%[text] # Symbolic Maneuver Planning for Orbital Rendezvous
%[text] This example derives closed-form maneuver planning equations for spacecraft proximity operations using the Clohessy-Wiltshire equations, then reuses those equations in downstream timing, safety, and sensitivity studies.
%[text] **Workflow:** Linear relative-motion ODEs -\> `dsolve` analytic solution -\> no-drift safety condition -\> transfer delta-v equations -\> `matlabFunction` code generation -\> timing sweep, trajectory visualization, sensitivity analysis, and a compact uncertainty check
%[text] Requires: Symbolic Math Toolbox™
%[text] Copyright 2026 The MathWorks, Inc.
%%
%[text] ## 1. The Clohessy-Wiltshire Equations
%[text] The Clohessy-Wiltshire (CW) equations describe relative motion of a chaser spacecraft with respect to a target in a circular reference orbit. The coordinate frame is the Local-Vertical/Local-Horizontal (LVLH) frame centered on the target:
%[text] - $x$ (R-bar): radial, outward from Earth center
%[text] - $y$ (V-bar): along-track, in the direction of orbital velocity
%[text] - $z$ (H-bar): cross-track, completing the right-hand frame \
%[text] For a circular reference orbit with mean motion $n = \\sqrt{\\mu/a^3}$, the linearized equations of relative motion are:
%[text] $\\ddot{x} - 2n\\dot{y} - 3n^2 x = 0$
%[text] $\\ddot{y} + 2n\\dot{x} = 0$
%[text] $\\ddot{z} + n^2 z = 0$
%[text] The in-plane ($x$-$y$) motion is coupled; cross-track ($z$) is independent.
syms n positive
syms t
% In-plane CW equations: x (radial), y (along-track)
syms x(t) y(t)
Dx = diff(x, t);
D2x = diff(x, t, 2);
Dy = diff(y, t);
D2y = diff(y, t, 2);
cw_x = D2x - 2*n*Dy - 3*n^2*x == 0;
cw_y = D2y + 2*n*Dx == 0;
% Cross-track CW equation: z (out-of-plane)
syms z(t)
Dz = diff(z, t);
D2z = diff(z, t, 2);
cw_z = D2z + n^2*z == 0;
%[text] Clohessy-Wiltshire equations:
cw_equations = [cw_x; cw_y; cw_z] %[output:27b9b383]
%%
%[text] ## 2. Analytic General Solution via `dsolve`
%[text] `dsolve` produces the exact closed-form solution of the coupled linear ODE system. The in-plane solution contains oscillatory terms plus the secular along-track drift term that matters for bounded proximity operations.
syms x0 y0 vx0 vy0 real
conds_xy = [x(0) == x0, y(0) == y0, Dx(0) == vx0, Dy(0) == vy0];
sol_xy = dsolve([cw_x, cw_y], conds_xy);
%[text] General in-plane solution $x(t)$:
x_sol = simplify(sol_xy.x) %[output:257cc0eb]
%[text] General in-plane solution $y(t)$:
y_sol = simplify(sol_xy.y) %[output:95c5b930]
syms z0 vz0 real
conds_z = [z(0) == z0, Dz(0) == vz0];
sol_z = dsolve(cw_z, conds_z);
%[text] Cross-track solution $z(t)$:
z_sol = simplify(sol_z) %[output:391a2d70]
%%
%[text] ### No-Drift Condition
%[text] The secular drift is the coefficient of the term that grows linearly with time. Dividing by $t$ and taking the limit removes the bounded sinusoidal terms and leaves the drift rate.
%[text] Along-track drift rate:
y_drift_rate = simplify(limit(y_sol/t, t, inf)) %[output:224f6338]
%[text] No-drift condition:
no_drift = solve(y_drift_rate == 0, vy0) %[output:37ef6c06]
%%
%[text] ## 3. Impulsive Maneuver Delta-V
%[text] The transfer problem is: given initial relative position $(x\_0,y\_0)$, desired final relative position $(x\_f,y\_f)$, and transfer time $T$, what initial relative velocity reaches the endpoint?
syms T positive
syms xf yf real
x_at_T = subs(x_sol, t, T);
y_at_T = subs(y_sol, t, T);
endpoint_eqs = [x_at_T == xf, y_at_T == yf];
vel_sol = solve(endpoint_eqs, [vx0, vy0]);
%[text] Required departure velocity $v\_{x0}(T,x\_0,y\_0,x\_f,y\_f)$:
vx_required = simplify(vel_sol.vx0) %[output:5ec9bb5f]
%[text] Required departure velocity $v\_{y0}(T,x\_0,y\_0,x\_f,y\_f)$:
vy_required = simplify(vel_sol.vy0) %[output:3a634e13]
%%
%[text] ### Delta-V Magnitude
%[text] For a chaser initially station-keeping, the departure delta-v is the required relative velocity magnitude. The arrival delta-v is the velocity at $t = T$ that must be removed to stop at the target point.
dv_depart = simplify(sqrt(vx_required^2 + vy_required^2)) %[output:82511de3]
vx_sol = diff(x_sol, t);
vy_sol = diff(y_sol, t);
vx_arrival = simplify(subs(vx_sol, [t, vx0, vy0], [T, vx_required, vy_required]));
vy_arrival = simplify(subs(vy_sol, [t, vx0, vy0], [T, vx_required, vy_required]));
dv_arrive = simplify(sqrt(vx_arrival^2 + vy_arrival^2));
dv_total = simplify(dv_depart + dv_arrive) %[output:54b24bd4]
%%
%[text] ## 4. Reference Mission
%[text] Use an ISS-like servicing scenario: the chaser starts 1 km behind and 50 m below the target docking port in a 420 km circular reference orbit.
mission.altitudeKm = 420;
mission.earthRadiusKm = 6371;
mission.muKm = 398600.4418;
mission.semiMajorAxisKm = mission.earthRadiusKm + mission.altitudeKm;
mission.meanMotion = sqrt(mission.muKm / mission.semiMajorAxisKm^3);
mission.period = 2*pi / mission.meanMotion;
mission.initialPosition = [-50; -1000];
mission.finalPosition = [0; 0];
printReferenceMission(mission) %[output:73204730]
%%
%[text] ## 5. Code Generation for Reuse
%[text] Convert symbolic expressions into optimized MATLAB® functions. These generated functions are the handoff point from first-principles derivation to repeated engineering analysis.
maneuverVars = {n, T, x0, y0, xf, yf};
matlabFunction(vx_required, vy_required, ...
    'File', 'departureVelocity', ...
    'Vars', maneuverVars, ...
    'Outputs', {'vx0_req', 'vy0_req'}, ...
    'Optimize', true);
matlabFunction(vx_arrival, vy_arrival, ...
    'File', 'arrivalVelocity', ...
    'Vars', maneuverVars, ...
    'Outputs', {'vx_arr', 'vy_arr'}, ...
    'Optimize', true);
matlabFunction(dv_depart, dv_arrive, ...
    'File', 'maneuverDeltaV', ...
    'Vars', maneuverVars, ...
    'Outputs', {'dv_dep', 'dv_arr'}, ...
    'Optimize', true);
trajectoryVars = {n, t, x0, y0, vx0, vy0};
matlabFunction(x_sol, y_sol, ...
    'File', 'cwTrajectory', ...
    'Vars', trajectoryVars, ...
    'Outputs', {'x_traj', 'y_traj'}, ...
    'Optimize', true);
fprintf(['Generated: departureVelocity.m\n' ... %[output:group:18f31d9e] %[output:878e8f47]
    'Generated: arrivalVelocity.m\n' ... %[output:878e8f47]
    'Generated: maneuverDeltaV.m\n' ... %[output:878e8f47]
    'Generated: cwTrajectory.m\n']) %[output:group:18f31d9e] %[output:878e8f47]
%%
%[text] ## 6. Fuel-Optimal Transfer Timing
%[text] The generated delta-v function evaluates the exact analytic expressions over thousands of transfer times in one vectorized call. Singular transfer times are marked and masked in the plot so the practical delta-v trade remains visible.
T_sweep = linspace(0.05*mission.period, 2*mission.period, 2000);
[dv_dep_sweep, dv_arr_sweep] = maneuverDeltaV(mission.meanMotion, T_sweep, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), ...
    mission.finalPosition(1), mission.finalPosition(2));
dv_total_sweep = dv_dep_sweep + dv_arr_sweep;
[optimal.dvTotal, optimal.index] = min(dv_total_sweep);
optimal.time = T_sweep(optimal.index);
optimal.dvDepart = dv_dep_sweep(optimal.index);
optimal.dvArrive = dv_arr_sweep(optimal.index);
plotDeltaVSweep(T_sweep, dv_dep_sweep, dv_arr_sweep, optimal, mission.meanMotion) %[output:7507f845]
printFuelOptimalTransfer(optimal, mission) %[output:63f8e00b]
%%
%[text] ### Optimal Transfer Trajectory
%[text] The same analytic trajectory solution becomes a reusable propagator after `matlabFunction`; here it evaluates the optimal transfer path directly.
[vx0_opt, vy0_opt] = departureVelocity(mission.meanMotion, optimal.time, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), ...
    mission.finalPosition(1), mission.finalPosition(2));
t_traj = linspace(0, optimal.time, 500);
[x_traj, y_traj] = cwTrajectory(mission.meanMotion, t_traj, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), vx0_opt, vy0_opt);
plotTransferTrajectory(x_traj, y_traj, vx0_opt, vy0_opt, optimal, mission) %[output:471c5c54]
%%
%[text] ## 7. Safety Ellipse Analysis
%[text] Substituting the no-drift condition into the symbolic solution gives the bounded relative-motion family. With zero radial velocity, the classical passive safety ellipse follows directly.
%[text] Bounded orbit $x(t)$ under $\\dot{y}\_0 = -2nx\_0$:
x_bounded = simplify(subs(x_sol, vy0, no_drift)) %[output:6fb61a14]
%[text] Bounded orbit $y(t)$ under $\\dot{y}\_0 = -2nx\_0$:
y_bounded = simplify(subs(y_sol, vy0, no_drift)) %[output:746fc886]
%[text] Pure hold case with $\\dot{x}\_0 = 0$:
x_pure_hold = simplify(subs(x_bounded, vx0, 0)) %[output:01a81102]
y_pure_hold = simplify(subs(y_bounded, vx0, 0)) %[output:86897343]
%[text] The symbolic identity below is the ellipse equation $x^2/x\_0^2 + (y-y\_0)^2/(2x\_0)^2 = 1$.
ellipse_identity = simplify(x_pure_hold^2/x0^2 + (y_pure_hold - y0)^2/(4*x0^2)) %[output:280d973d]
radial_semiaxis = abs(x0);
along_track_semiaxis = 2*abs(x0);
%%
%[text] ### Visualize Safety Ellipses
%[text] The visualization is bookkeeping, so the plotting code is kept in a helper function while the symbolic ellipse derivation remains visible above.
plotSafetyEllipses(mission) %[output:4b4575aa]
%%
%[text] ## 8. Sensitivity Analysis
%[text] Symbolic differentiation gives the exact Jacobian from departure velocity error to arrival position error. This is the local linear map that mission designers use to reason about burn execution sensitivity.
J_pos_vel = simplify(jacobian([x_at_T; y_at_T], [vx0, vy0]));
%[text] Maneuver sensitivity matrix $\\partial(x\_f,y\_f)/\\partial(v\_{x0},v\_{y0})$:
J_pos_vel %[output:5f9ac800]
matlabFunction(J_pos_vel, ...
    'File', 'maneuverSensitivity', ...
    'Vars', {n, T}, ...
    'Outputs', {'J'}, ...
    'Optimize', true);
fprintf('Generated: maneuverSensitivity.m\n') %[output:3b239366]
%%
%[text] ### Sensitivity Across Transfer Time
%[text] Reusing the generated sensitivity function over the same timing grid shows how departure burn errors are amplified by transfer timing. The selected fuel-optimal transfer time is marked for context.
J_opt = maneuverSensitivity(mission.meanMotion, optimal.time);
printSensitivitySummary(J_opt, optimal) %[output:2793d193]
J_sweep = arrayfun(@(time) maneuverSensitivity(mission.meanMotion, time), T_sweep, ...
    'UniformOutput', false);
worst_amp = cellfun(@(J) max(svd(J)), J_sweep);
plotSensitivitySweep(T_sweep, worst_amp, optimal, mission.meanMotion) %[output:763db783]
%%
%[text] ## 9. Compact Uncertainty Reuse Check
%[text] A small Monte Carlo check shows another downstream use of the generated equations. It is intentionally framed as a reuse demonstration, not as a claim that this simple two-impulse transfer meets final docking dispersions.
scenarioCount = 2000;
sigmaVelocity = 0.01/3;  % 1 cm/s at 3-sigma, per velocity axis
dispersion = runVelocityErrorMonteCarlo(mission, optimal, sigmaVelocity, scenarioCount);
printDispersionSummary(dispersion) %[output:08d0f6ea]
plotDispersionMonteCarlo(dispersion) %[output:9db3c777]
%%
%[text] ## Helper Functions
%[text] The helper functions below keep plotting, reporting, and random sampling out of the symbolic derivation path.
function printReferenceMission(mission)
arguments
    mission (1,1) struct
end
fprintf(['=== Reference Mission: ISS Proximity Operations ===\n' ...
    'Orbit altitude:      %d km\n' ...
    'Semi-major axis:     %.1f km\n' ...
    'Mean motion:         %.6f rad/s\n' ...
    'Orbital period:      %.1f min\n' ...
    'Start position:      (%.0f, %.0f) m  [R-bar, V-bar]\n' ...
    'Target position:     (%.0f, %.0f) m  [origin]\n'], ...
    mission.altitudeKm, ...
    mission.semiMajorAxisKm, ...
    mission.meanMotion, ...
    mission.period/60, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), ...
    mission.finalPosition(1), mission.finalPosition(2))
end
function plotDeltaVSweep(T_sweep, dv_dep_sweep, dv_arr_sweep, optimal, meanMotion)
arguments
    T_sweep (1,:) double
    dv_dep_sweep (1,:) double
    dv_arr_sweep (1,:) double
    optimal (1,1) struct
    meanMotion (1,1) double {mustBePositive}
end
dvTotalSweep = dv_dep_sweep + dv_arr_sweep;
[plotMask, singularTimes] = transferPlotMask(T_sweep, dvTotalSweep, optimal, meanMotion);
dvDepPlot = dv_dep_sweep;
dvArrPlot = dv_arr_sweep;
dvTotalPlot = dvTotalSweep;
dvDepPlot(~plotMask) = NaN;
dvArrPlot(~plotMask) = NaN;
dvTotalPlot(~plotMask) = NaN;
plot(T_sweep/60, dvDepPlot, 'b-', 'LineWidth', 1.5)
hold on
plot(T_sweep/60, dvArrPlot, 'r--', 'LineWidth', 1.5)
plot(T_sweep/60, dvTotalPlot, 'k-', 'LineWidth', 2)
plot(optimal.time/60, optimal.dvTotal, 'go', 'MarkerSize', 10, 'MarkerFaceColor', 'g')
for idx = 1:numel(singularTimes)
    xline(singularTimes(idx)/60, 'k:', 'Singular', ...
        'HandleVisibility', 'off', ...
        'LabelOrientation', 'horizontal', ...
        'LabelVerticalAlignment', 'bottom')
end
hold off
xlabel('Transfer time [min]')
ylabel('\Delta v [m/s]')
title('Two-Impulse Rendezvous \Delta v vs. Transfer Time')
legend('Departure \Delta v', 'Arrival \Delta v', ...
    sprintf('Total (min = %.3f m/s at T = %.1f min)', optimal.dvTotal, optimal.time/60), ...
    'Optimal', 'Location', 'best')
ylim([0, practicalDeltaVLimit(dvTotalSweep, plotMask, optimal)])
grid on
end
function [plotMask, singularTimes] = transferPlotMask(T_sweep, dvTotalSweep, optimal, meanMotion)
arguments
    T_sweep (1,:) double
    dvTotalSweep (1,:) double
    optimal (1,1) struct
    meanMotion (1,1) double {mustBePositive}
end
theta = meanMotion*T_sweep;
transferDenominator = 8*cos(theta) + 3*theta.*sin(theta) - 8;
denominatorMask = abs(transferDenominator) > 0.1;
finiteMask = isfinite(dvTotalSweep);
initialMask = finiteMask & denominatorMask;
plotLimit = practicalDeltaVLimit(dvTotalSweep, initialMask, optimal);
plotMask = initialMask & (dvTotalSweep <= plotLimit);
singularTimes = findTransferSingularities(T_sweep, meanMotion);
end
function upperLimit = practicalDeltaVLimit(dvTotalSweep, plotMask, optimal)
arguments
    dvTotalSweep (1,:) double
    plotMask (1,:) logical
    optimal (1,1) struct
end
validDeltaV = dvTotalSweep(plotMask & isfinite(dvTotalSweep) & dvTotalSweep > 0);
if isempty(validDeltaV)
    upperLimit = 10*optimal.dvTotal;
else
    upperLimit = max(1.25*prctile(validDeltaV, 98), 5*optimal.dvTotal);
end
end
function singularTimes = findTransferSingularities(T_sweep, meanMotion)
arguments
    T_sweep (1,:) double
    meanMotion (1,1) double {mustBePositive}
end
thetaRange = meanMotion*[min(T_sweep), max(T_sweep)];
thetaGrid = linspace(thetaRange(1), thetaRange(2), 5000);
denominator = @(theta) 8*cos(theta) + 3*theta.*sin(theta) - 8;
denominatorValues = denominator(thetaGrid);
crossingIdx = find(denominatorValues(1:end-1).*denominatorValues(2:end) <= 0);
singularTheta = zeros(1, 0);
for idx = crossingIdx
    thetaLeft = thetaGrid(idx);
    thetaRight = thetaGrid(idx + 1);
    valueLeft = denominatorValues(idx);
    valueRight = denominatorValues(idx + 1);
    if valueLeft == 0
        thetaRoot = thetaLeft;
    elseif valueRight == 0
        thetaRoot = thetaRight;
    else
        thetaRoot = fzero(denominator, [thetaLeft, thetaRight]);
    end
    if isempty(singularTheta) || all(abs(thetaRoot - singularTheta) > 1e-5)
        singularTheta(end + 1) = thetaRoot; %#ok<AGROW>
    end
end
endpointTheta = thetaRange(abs(denominator(thetaRange)) < 1e-8);
for thetaRoot = endpointTheta
    if isempty(singularTheta) || all(abs(thetaRoot - singularTheta) > 1e-5)
        singularTheta(end + 1) = thetaRoot; %#ok<AGROW>
    end
end
singularTimes = sort(singularTheta/meanMotion);
end
function printFuelOptimalTransfer(optimal, mission)
arguments
    optimal (1,1) struct
    mission (1,1) struct
end
fprintf(['\n=== Fuel-Optimal Transfer ===\n' ...
    'Optimal transfer time: %.1f min (%.2f orbits)\n' ...
    'Departure delta-v:     %.4f m/s\n' ...
    'Arrival delta-v:       %.4f m/s\n' ...
    'Total delta-v:         %.4f m/s\n'], ...
    optimal.time/60, optimal.time/mission.period, ...
    optimal.dvDepart, optimal.dvArrive, optimal.dvTotal)
end
function plotTransferTrajectory(x_traj, y_traj, vx0_opt, vy0_opt, optimal, mission)
arguments
    x_traj (1,:) double
    y_traj (1,:) double
    vx0_opt (1,1) double
    vy0_opt (1,1) double
    optimal (1,1) struct
    mission (1,1) struct
end
plot(y_traj, x_traj, 'b-', 'LineWidth', 2)
hold on
plot(mission.initialPosition(2), mission.initialPosition(1), 'bs', ...
    'MarkerSize', 12, 'MarkerFaceColor', 'b')
plot(mission.finalPosition(2), mission.finalPosition(1), 'r^', ...
    'MarkerSize', 12, 'MarkerFaceColor', 'r')
quiver(mission.initialPosition(2), mission.initialPosition(1), vy0_opt*100, vx0_opt*100, 0, ...
    'b', 'LineWidth', 2, 'MaxHeadSize', 0.5)
hold off
xlabel('V-bar (along-track) [m]')
ylabel('R-bar (radial) [m]')
title(sprintf('Optimal Transfer: T = %.1f min, \\Delta v = %.3f m/s', ...
    optimal.time/60, optimal.dvTotal))
legend('Transfer trajectory', 'Chaser start', 'Target', 'Departure \Delta v', ...
    'Location', 'best')
set(gca, 'XDir', 'reverse')
grid on
axis equal
end
function plotSafetyEllipses(mission)
arguments
    mission (1,1) struct
end
holdDistances = [-200, -100, -50];
radialOffsets = [-30, -20, -10];
tEllipse = linspace(0, mission.period, 500);
colors = lines(numel(holdDistances));
hold on
for idx = 1:numel(holdDistances)
    x0Hold = radialOffsets(idx);
    y0Hold = holdDistances(idx);
    vy0Hold = -2*mission.meanMotion*x0Hold;
    [xEllipse, yEllipse] = cwTrajectory(mission.meanMotion, tEllipse, ...
        x0Hold, y0Hold, 0, vy0Hold);
    plot(yEllipse, xEllipse, '-', 'Color', colors(idx,:), 'LineWidth', 2, ...
        'DisplayName', sprintf('Hold: (%.0f, %.0f) m', x0Hold, y0Hold))
    plot(y0Hold, x0Hold, 'o', 'Color', colors(idx,:), ...
        'MarkerSize', 8, 'MarkerFaceColor', colors(idx,:), ...
        'HandleVisibility', 'off')
end
plot(0, 0, 'r^', 'MarkerSize', 14, 'MarkerFaceColor', 'r', ...
    'DisplayName', 'Target')
hold off
xlabel('V-bar (along-track) [m]')
ylabel('R-bar (radial) [m]')
title('CW Safety Ellipses: Bounded Relative Orbits')
legend('Location', 'eastoutside')
set(gca, 'XDir', 'reverse')
grid on
axis equal
end
function printSensitivitySummary(J_opt, optimal)
arguments
    J_opt (2,2) double
    optimal (1,1) struct
end
singularValues = svd(J_opt);
fprintf(['\n=== Maneuver Sensitivity at T = %.1f min ===\n' ...
    'Sensitivity matrix [m per m/s]:\n' ...
    '  [%8.2f  %8.2f]\n' ...
    '  [%8.2f  %8.2f]\n' ...
    'Singular values: %.2f, %.2f m/(m/s)\n' ...
    'Worst-case: 1 cm/s error -> %.2f m miss distance\n' ...
    'Best-case:  1 cm/s error -> %.2f m miss distance\n'], ...
    optimal.time/60, ...
    J_opt(1,1), J_opt(1,2), ...
    J_opt(2,1), J_opt(2,2), ...
    singularValues(1), singularValues(2), ...
    singularValues(1)*0.01, singularValues(2)*0.01)
end
function plotSensitivitySweep(T_sweep, worst_amp, optimal, meanMotion)
arguments
    T_sweep (1,:) double
    worst_amp (1,:) double
    optimal (1,1) struct
    meanMotion (1,1) double {mustBePositive}
end
singularTimes = findTransferSingularities(T_sweep, meanMotion);
plot(T_sweep/60, worst_amp*0.01, 'r-', 'LineWidth', 1.5)
hold on
xline(optimal.time/60, 'g--', 'Selected T', ...
    'LineWidth', 1.5, ...
    'LabelOrientation', 'horizontal', ...
    'LabelVerticalAlignment', 'bottom')
for idx = 1:numel(singularTimes)
    xline(singularTimes(idx)/60, 'k:', 'Singular', ...
        'HandleVisibility', 'off', ...
        'LabelOrientation', 'horizontal', ...
        'LabelVerticalAlignment', 'top')
end
hold off
xlabel('Transfer time [min]')
ylabel('Worst-case miss per 1 cm/s error [m]')
title('Arrival Sensitivity from Symbolic Jacobian')
grid on
end
function dispersion = runVelocityErrorMonteCarlo(mission, optimal, sigmaVelocity, scenarioCount)
arguments
    mission (1,1) struct
    optimal (1,1) struct
    sigmaVelocity (1,1) double {mustBePositive}
    scenarioCount (1,1) double {mustBeInteger, mustBePositive}
end
rng(42)
[vxNominal, vyNominal] = departureVelocity(mission.meanMotion, optimal.time, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), ...
    mission.finalPosition(1), mission.finalPosition(2));
velocityErrors = sigmaVelocity*randn(scenarioCount, 2);
vxSamples = vxNominal + velocityErrors(:,1);
vySamples = vyNominal + velocityErrors(:,2);
[xFinal, yFinal] = cwTrajectory(mission.meanMotion, optimal.time, ...
    mission.initialPosition(1), mission.initialPosition(2), vxSamples, vySamples);
missRadial = xFinal - mission.finalPosition(1);
missAlong = yFinal - mission.finalPosition(2);
missDistance = sqrt(missRadial.^2 + missAlong.^2);
J = maneuverSensitivity(mission.meanMotion, optimal.time);
positionCovariance = J*(sigmaVelocity^2*eye(2))*J';
[eigVectors, eigValues] = eig(positionCovariance);
[semiAxes, order] = sort(3*sqrt(diag(eigValues)), 'descend');
eigVectors = eigVectors(:, order);
theta = linspace(0, 2*pi, 200);
ellipsePoints = eigVectors*diag(semiAxes)*[cos(theta); sin(theta)];
dispersion.transferTime = optimal.time;
dispersion.sigmaVelocity = sigmaVelocity;
dispersion.scenarioCount = scenarioCount;
dispersion.nominalVelocity = [vxNominal; vyNominal];
dispersion.missRadial = missRadial;
dispersion.missAlong = missAlong;
dispersion.missDistance = missDistance;
dispersion.semiAxes = semiAxes;
dispersion.ellipsePoints = ellipsePoints;
end
function printDispersionSummary(dispersion)
arguments
    dispersion (1,1) struct
end
fprintf(['\n=== Compact Velocity-Error Reuse Check ===\n' ...
    'Transfer time:                    %.1f min\n' ...
    'Scenarios:                        %d\n' ...
    'Velocity error, 3-sigma per axis: %.4f m/s\n' ...
    'Nominal departure velocity:       (%.4f, %.4f) m/s\n' ...
    'Mean miss distance:               %.3f m\n' ...
    '99th percentile miss distance:    %.3f m\n' ...
    'Analytic 3-sigma semi-axes:       %.3f m, %.3f m\n'], ...
    dispersion.transferTime/60, ...
    dispersion.scenarioCount, ...
    3*dispersion.sigmaVelocity, ...
    dispersion.nominalVelocity(1), dispersion.nominalVelocity(2), ...
    mean(dispersion.missDistance), ...
    quantile(dispersion.missDistance, 0.99), ...
    dispersion.semiAxes(1), dispersion.semiAxes(2))
end
function plotDispersionMonteCarlo(dispersion)
arguments
    dispersion (1,1) struct
end
tiledlayout(1, 1)
nexttile
scatter(dispersion.missAlong, dispersion.missRadial, 6, dispersion.missDistance, ...
    'filled', 'MarkerFaceAlpha', 0.3)
hold on
plot(dispersion.ellipsePoints(2,:), dispersion.ellipsePoints(1,:), 'r-', 'LineWidth', 2)
plot(0, 0, 'r^', 'MarkerSize', 14, 'MarkerFaceColor', 'r')
hold off
colorbar
colormap(parula)
xlabel('V-bar miss [m]')
ylabel('R-bar miss [m]')
title(sprintf('Arrival Dispersion (%d scenarios, 3\\sigma = %.3f m/s)', ...
    dispersion.scenarioCount, 3*dispersion.sigmaVelocity))
legend('Monte Carlo', '3\sigma ellipse (analytic)', 'Docking port', ...
    'Location', 'best')
grid on
axis equal
end

